browser support (parked until the Vite work has landed)
- Goal: work on older tablets and phones, not just current Safari/Chrome, as others will use it.
  Target: Safari/iOS 15.4, which covers every device that can run iOS/iPadOS 15.8 (iPad Air 2,
  mini 4, the 2017 iPad, iPhone 6s/7/SE 1st gen). Lower (iOS 12 to 14, e.g. iPad Air 1) would
  need a legacy polyfill build: not worth it unless asked. .browserslistrc still says Safari 17.5,
  Chrome 120: it was set for one person's modern devices
- Until Vite is in, the real floor is Safari 16.4, because pages use an import map (the Vite
  production build bundles the code, so the import maps go). So: do this after the Vite work,
  and set .browserslistrc to the agreed floor then, not before
- Then: handle the 42 color-mix() uses (Safari 16.2): 20 are `color-mix(in srgb, currentColor
  N%, transparent)`, which a fallback colour or an opacity will do; the other 22 mix a theme
  colour (danger 9, success 7, primary 4, warning 2), so they need derived theme variables
  (e.g. --color-danger-tint) in theme-manager; check .at(), structuredClone,
  crypto.randomUUID and dialog use against 15.4; make the service worker classic (not a module)
  for old Android Chrome, if Vite can emit it; update the README line "targets recent browsers
  only" and the browser line in CLAUDE.md
- Core is setlist navigation (reading and moving through the setlist, offline). The media player
  is optional and may be off on older devices: it is not loaded when the device has no Web Audio
  or it is switched off in Preferences (media-player-loader.js), and a player that fails to load
  is a warning, not an error. Don't make the core depend on it
- Usage pattern to design for: a dedicated iPad opened every 3 to 4 weeks, often old, often on
  poor wifi. So: the app must open offline from its cache (needs the full precache from the Vite
  work), data must survive the weeks between (the install nag, below), and a signed-in session
  and the Drive link must still work after weeks (test an expired token with no network: local
  setlists must still show)
- Already done: no Popover API (menu, song settings, key/capo picker are modal <dialog>s via
  DialogPopup), no CSS nesting, no Navigation API
- Needs a real old iPad (an iPad 5th gen on iPadOS 16.7 is the best single test) or a device
  service: Playwright's WebKit is current, so it can't show old-Safari problems. View
  transitions are Safari 18+, so older iPads simply don't animate between views (fine)

navigation
- When the supported browsers all have the Navigation API (Safari/iOS 26.2, Firefox 147, Chrome
  102), rewrite AppRouter on it and delete the code the platform then does: link interception,
  popstate, history entry keys and the view state in sessionStorage (use the entry's state), and
  the scroll/focus handling. Keep AppRouter the only place that knows. No polyfill for now:
  @virtualstate/navigation is still alpha (last release Oct 2025), doesn't intercept link clicks
  (so we'd keep that code), and passes 139 of 306 web-platform tests

